menu "Camera module SDK (KDCMR001)"

    config CAMERA_AO_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the module's owner (0: KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH)"
        range 0 24
        default 0
        help
            The QP/C priority of the Active Object that owns the Camera
            module, which is also its task's FreeRTOS priority. 0 takes
            kode-sdk's KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH; camera_ao.c says why. Two Active
            Objects at one level stop the board when the second starts, so
            an app whose own Active Object needs KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH moves
            this one to a level nothing in its image holds.

    config CAMERA_LAB
        bool "Laboratory build: any register of the sensor"
        default n
        help
            Opens what the register lock closes: camera_lab_register_write() writes
            any register of the sensor, locked or not, and CAMERA_NIGHT (the
            sensor's night mode, which stretches frames past their period)
            can be set.

            A build with this on can change the module's clocks, its frame
            timing and its pads, so the frame rate and the
            SDK's timings no longer describe it. It is for experiments with
            the sensor's registers, and nothing else. Never ship an app built
            with it.

endmenu
